factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 6 problems
  The draft says the van was stopped and checked at Musiri Kaveri bridge, but the article says the van was checked near Musiri Kaveri bridge; the draft's reel_script and slides say the van was caught there, which is broadly consistent, but the caption places the van at the same bridge while the article only says 'near' (minor). More clearly: the reel_script states the policeman 'Marudhamuthu' was 'ஓட்டிய' the van, which matches, but the reel_script omits the key fact that the van owner Manikavasagam requested to remove the bananas before the van was taken and that the SSI Vadivel ordered the van taken to the station, a material cause of the incident that is missing from the reel_script.
  The reel_script says the driver 'vijay' was drunk, which the article supports, but the draft never names the driver Vijay; this is an omission rather than an error.
  The caption says the owner Manikavasagam is 45 years old; the article gives his age as 45, which is correct, so this is not a problem.
  The caption and reel_script describe the policeman as being told to drive the van by 'இடம்' (place) instead of by SSI Vadivel; the caption's sentence 'போலீஸ்காரர் மருதமுத்து (40 வயது), இடம் கூறப்பட்டது' is ungrammatical and has no clear meaning in Tamil.
  The caption's date 'நவம்பர் 26, 2026 (இரவு)' is treated as the posting date and is excluded, but the caption also labels the time as 'இரவு' (night) in a way that attributes the timing to the article's event; the article only says the van left on the night before the incident, so the time label is not clearly supported.
  The reel_script and slides say the van was 'பிடிக்கப்பட்டது' (caught) and that the policeman was injured after the van was taken to the station, but they omit that the van owner's request to take out the bananas was refused by SSI Vadivel, which is an important cause of the incident missing from the reel_script.
